<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trave</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trave is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which flows past Bad Segeberg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a> at Travemünde. Lübeck was refounded in 1159 on a hill between the Trave and the Wakenitz, and the river gave the city the access to the sea that made it the leading port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trave.jpg" alt="Trave" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bryan Rutherford · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elbe%E2%80%93L%C3%BCbeck_Canal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
